# URmessage — line-ending and diff policy for the whole tree.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE FIRST FILE IN THE REPOSITORY, ON PURPOSE.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is set at SYSTEM scope on the development box, which
# means git will happily rewrite LF -> CRLF on checkout for anything it decides
# is "text". Its decision is a heuristic over the first 8000 bytes. An OpenType
# or TrueType font that trips that heuristic is silently corrupted on checkout —
# and a corrupt font produces NO error anywhere: DirectWrite simply fails to
# register the family, XAML falls back to a system face, and the app renders in
# the wrong typeface with a clean build log. The URnetwork VPN repo learned this
# with an Assets/-only .gitattributes; that scope is not enough, so this one is
# top-level and explicit in both directions.
#
# Policy:
#   1. Default is NO conversion (`-text`). An unrecognised file is never
#      rewritten. This is the safe default: the failure mode of leaving a text
#      file alone is cosmetic, the failure mode of rewriting a binary is silent
#      corruption.
#   2. Source text is named explicitly and normalised to LF in the repository.
#   3. Binaries are named explicitly as `binary` (= `-text -diff`), so they can
#      never be converted and never be diffed as text.
#
# Verify after any clone/checkout on Windows with:
#   git ls-files --eol
# Fonts and icons must read `w/-text` (no working-tree eol conversion).

# ---- 1. default: touch nothing -------------------------------------------
*                   -text

# ---- 2. text sources: LF in the repo and in the working tree --------------
*.c                 text eol=lf
*.cc                text eol=lf
*.cpp               text eol=lf
*.h                 text eol=lf
*.hpp               text eol=lf
*.idl               text eol=lf
*.rc                text eol=lf diff=cpp
*.xaml              text eol=lf
*.xml               text eol=lf
*.resw              text eol=lf
*.manifest          text eol=lf
*.vcxproj           text eol=lf
*.vcxproj.filters   text eol=lf
*.props             text eol=lf
*.targets           text eol=lf
*.config            text eol=lf
*.sln               text eol=lf
*.ps1               text eol=lf
*.psm1              text eol=lf
*.sh                text eol=lf
*.py                text eol=lf
*.md                text eol=lf
*.txt               text eol=lf
*.json              text eol=lf
*.yml               text eol=lf
*.yaml              text eol=lf
*.gitattributes     text eol=lf
*.gitignore         text eol=lf
.gitattributes      text eol=lf
.gitignore          text eol=lf

# ---- 3. binaries: never converted, never diffed as text -------------------
# Brand faces. These are the reason this file exists (see the header) and they
# are ALSO commercially licensed — do not redistribute them outside the app.
*.otf               binary
*.ttf               binary
*.ttc               binary
*.woff              binary
*.woff2             binary
*.eot               binary
# Icons and images
*.ico               binary
*.png               binary
*.jpg               binary
*.jpeg              binary
*.gif               binary
*.bmp               binary
*.webp              binary
*.svgz              binary
*.icns              binary
# Compiled / packaged / archived
*.pri               binary
*.exe               binary
*.dll               binary
*.lib               binary
*.pdb               binary
*.winmd             binary
*.msi               binary
*.msix              binary
*.nupkg             binary
*.zip               binary
*.7z                binary
*.gz                binary
*.pfx               binary
*.cer               binary
*.snk               binary
